t right up to the end, and I’m really glad it’s out.So nobody goes in with the wrong expectations: almost nothing in this demo is final. It’s meant to give you a general feel for how SuperCitycon looks and plays, and that’s about it. For example, there’s no economy in the game yet. You can build and explore, but it isn’t a “real” city builder yet, with systems that feed into each other and goals","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-14T22:47:25Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706675798","verified_at":"2026-10-20T11:09:29Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-3474890-1842846814455135","game_id":"steam-3474890","kind":"announcement","title":"Why Is It Called SuperCitycon?","summary":"Back in 2017, when my gamedev journey started, the game didn't really have a name. The project was simply called City, and for more than two and a half years, that was all it was called. No clever working title, no grand plan for the final name, just City. In fact, the original project folder is still called City to this day.The name Citycon came much later, almost by accident. At some point during development, I was building what is now called the Citycon Building, the city's construction yard.","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-08T09:36:59Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1842846814455135","verified_at":"2026-10-20T11:09:29Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-3474890":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-25T18:43:10Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-25T18:43:10Z","error_codes":[]}},"news_last_attempt_at":{"steam-3474890":"2026-10-25T18:43:10Z"},"notices":[],"news_sources":{"3474890":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-25T18:43:10Z","last_success_at":"2026-1